[#:seon.task{:name "a-host-bound-change-has-no-proof-from-the-repl"
             :plan "A branch's change to a host-bound function runs its tests on the old compiled Var, so `seon.cluster.branch-evidence/branch-evidence` refuses it and only `bin/seon check --test` proves it. `my.test/check-platform` writes the branch into a copy of the published archive (`my.program/write-branch!`), commits it on the published commit (`seon.test.platform/candidate-commit!`), runs the tests in a throwaway JVM (`seon.test.platform/run-check!`) and records their results on the branch (`seon.test.platform/record!`) as a run carrying `:seon.test.run/git-sha`; the gate then lists the change under `:seon.test.platform/proven`. Read `seon.test.runner/commit-results!`, `seon.test/verified?`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-09/platform-step.md` and `docs/seon/schedule/cards/PLATFORM-STEP.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-the-branch-adds-is-not-eligible-in-the-check"
             :plan "`my.test/check-platform` cannot prove a test the branch adds. Observed (default fa92a2503, 2026-10-09) added `my.program-test/an-agent-reads-and-writes-files-as-clojure-does` on its branch; write-back into candidate 84cf0c36c was correct, but the check refused \"The requested test is not eligible.\" (`seon.test/select`): the check store is cloned from the published commit's template (`seon.operator/seeded-store!`) and the candidate's files are published but not adopted (the run says \"source ... is published but not yet adopted\"), so the new test has no entity there. An existing test named the same way ran (run 2f3c6f610ea1). Done when a check-platform run naming a test only the branch declares runs it in the candidate JVM. Read `seon.test.platform/run-check!`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-refused-platform-check-names-no-diagnostic"
             :plan "A red or refused `bin/seon check` reached through `seon.test.platform/run-check!` answers only its argv and the first message line; the operator wrote a DIAGNOSTIC file (phases, test summary, failure reports) that the REPL answer does not name, so lane repl-only-a5 had to rerun the check from a shell to see why it failed. Done when the answer carries the diagnostic's test summary and phases as data."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-schema-resource-change-cannot-be-proven-by-check-platform"
             :plan "`my.test/check-platform` writes only the branch's declarations into a copy of the published archive (`seon.test.platform/snapshot!`), so a host-bound change that needs a schema resource beside it (A5: `:seon.sci.binding/target` entries in resources/seon/schemas/seon.sci.binding.edn read by `seon.sci.eval/build-base-ctx`) cannot be proven from the REPL: the candidate lacks the resource, and no REPL call puts a schema resource on a branch. Observed (2026-10-09) edited the resource by `my.edit/exact!` and proved the slice through `bin/lane commit --test` instead. Done when a branch can carry a schema-resource change that check-platform's candidate includes, with a regression."}
 #:seon.task{:name "platform-code-has-no-repl-proof-path-lanes-use"
             :plan "A compiled (host-bound) change cannot be proven at the REPL; loop-impl-flow (aca57cc39, a76a2baa4, 2026-10-10) proved its `seon.flow` and `seon.turn` slices only through `bin/seon check` after writing files, never through a branch. `my.test/check-platform` (fa92a2503) exists for exactly this and was not used. What blocked it: a schema-resource change cannot ride (`seon.test.platform/a-schema-resource-change-cannot-be-proven-by-check-platform`), a test the branch adds is not eligible (`seon.test.platform/a-test-the-branch-adds-is-not-eligible-in-the-check`), a refusal names no diagnostic (`seon.test.platform/a-refused-platform-check-names-no-diagnostic`), and it takes about 120 s, which an agent must know to pass as `timeout_ms`. Done when a host-bound slice of a lane (a `seon.flow` step) is proven by `my.test/check-platform` on its branch and committed through `bin/lane commit --branch-evidence`, the run recorded as the gate's `:seon.test.platform/proven`, and AGENT guidance says to use it first. Read `seon.cluster.branch-evidence/branch-evidence`, `seon.test.platform/record!`, `seon.test.platform/run-check!` and `docs/seon/schedule/cards/PLATFORM-STEP.md`."}]
